# kernel (Settings, About): src/kern.c, scripts/kernel.sh
about.kernel = Kernel
kern.stock = Sony (stock)
kern.eris47 = Project Eris v47
kern.mmc2019 = ModMyClassic 2019
kern.other = Not the stock kernel
kern.unknown = Checking the kernel…
kern.is_stock = This is the stock kernel and there is no copy of another one to go back to
kern.why = Wi-Fi and the network cable need Sony's kernel. The console keeps it intact in its recovery partition: it is copied from there, nothing is downloaded.
kern.rb_why = There is a copy of the previous kernel on the USB drive: you can go back to it. Wi-Fi and the network cable will stop working with that kernel.
kern.step1 = Backup to the USB drive, checked: the whole firmware the first time (a few minutes) and the current kernel
kern.step2 = Write Sony's kernel to the internal memory (under a second)
kern.rb_step2 = Write the previous kernel from the USB copy (under a second)
kern.step3 = Check; if anything differs, the copy is written back at once
kern.warn = If the power is cut during the write, the console may not start again. It is recovered by writing the copy from step 1 from a computer, over USB: keep it off the USB drive too. Do not turn off or unplug the console until it is done. Guide: lpsx.dev/recovery
kern.undo = It can be undone: on this same screen, “Go back to the previous kernel” writes the copy again.
kern.rb_note = Sony's kernel is copied first as well.
kern.running = Do not turn off or unplug the console: writing to the internal memory.
kern.restore_btn = Back up and restore
kern.rollback_btn = Go back to the previous kernel
kern.later = Later
kern.reboot = Restart now
kern.close = Close
kern.done_title = Sony's kernel restored
kern.done_rb_title = Previous kernel restored
kern.done_note = It is used from the next start.
kern.backup_at = USB / lumen / backup / kernel / {f}
kern.copy_note = Copy it to a computer: it is the only way to recover the console if the kernel ever fails to start. Guide: lpsx.dev/recovery
kern.err_title = Nothing was changed
kern.err_write_title = The write did not check out
kern.err_revert_title = Warning: the kernel may be damaged
kern.err_same = That kernel is already on the console.
kern.err_space = No room on the USB drive for the copy (8 MB needed).
kern.err_backup = The copy on the USB drive could not be checked: nothing was written.
kern.err_boot2 = The recovery partition does not hold Sony's original kernel: LPSX will not write anything.
kern.err_image = The backup file is not a valid kernel image.
kern.err_write = The previous kernel was written back and checked: the console is as before.
kern.err_revert = Do not turn off the console. Copy lumen/backup/kernel to a computer: it is needed to recover it over USB. Guide: lpsx.dev/recovery
kern.err_root = LPSX may not write the kernel.
kern.err_other = It could not be completed. See lumen/logs/kernel-restore.log.
kern.locked = Test option: create the file lumen/kernel-write-ok on the USB drive to enable it
